# Location check-in protocol

When the user says they rode somewhere or asks to update their location:

1. Run `node scripts/apply-location-stash.js --place "..."` immediately
2. Calculate distance from previous location via OSRM bicycle routing
3. Update `dayNumber` (increment by 1) and `kmRidden` (add today's distance) in `trip-data.js`
4. Add a `locationHistory` entry and an `updates` entry
5. Download any photos provided, extract EXIF timestamps, assign captions and pin coordinates
6. Generate route JSON, wire into `index.html` and `sw.js`
7. Commit and push everything

Never skip steps. Never ask the user for information that can be derived from OSRM or EXIF data.
